  "title": "MILimbEEG: Motor and motor-imagery limb EEG dataset (MILimbEEG)",
  "description": "MILimbEEG is an EEG dataset from 60 volunteers performing and imagining upper- and lower-limb movements (hand closing and dorsal/plantar foot flexion, left and right), plus baseline eyes-open and rest conditions. It comprises over 8,680 four-second recordings acquired with a 16-channel dry-electrode OpenBCI Cyton+Daisy system at 125 Hz. The cohort includes healthy participants and some clinical cases, such as amputees and post-COVID-19 participants. The dataset supports brain-computer interface research on motor execution and motor imagery.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a 16-channel OpenBCI Cyton+Daisy dry-electrode system at 125 Hz (10-10 montage, neutral ear reference), with hardware band-pass filtering at 5-50 Hz and a 60 Hz notch. In each repetition, participants executed and then imagined hand closing and foot flexion in cue-based four-second trials, with baseline eyes-open and rest periods.",
